# ===== Quest Zone — environment variable placeholders =====
#
# This project currently has NO server-side secrets and no build step —
# it's a static site (assets/js/qz-config.js hardcodes the Supabase
# project URL and PUBLIC publishable/anon key directly, which is the
# correct, intended way to ship them: they're safe to expose, Row Level
# Security is what actually protects data, not hiding this key).
#
# This file exists for the future: if a server-side component is ever
# added (a Supabase Edge Function, a build step, a CI job) that needs a
# real secret, it must be read from an environment variable — never
# hardcoded into a committed file — and its real value belongs in a local
# .env (already git-ignored, see .gitignore) or in that platform's own
# secrets manager (e.g. `supabase secrets set` for Edge Functions, GitHub
# Actions "Secrets" for a workflow), never here.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values ONLY if/when such a
# component actually exists. Never commit the real .env.

# Example shape for a future Edge Function needing the Supabase
# service-role key — SECURITY CRITICAL: this key must only ever be read
# by trusted server-side code (an Edge Function), NEVER by frontend code,
# and never committed anywhere:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Example shape for a future SMTP/email integration:
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
